#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Move the pins in src/nullbill/data/pins.yaml to what each vendor offers
as its newest stable release (docs/adr/0022-latest-stable.md).

    tools/pins list             what is pinned now
    tools/pins latest [NAME..]  what the vendors offer, changing nothing
    tools/pins bump [NAME..]    write the newer pins into their files

Every new pin comes with the vendor's own checksum, checked here against
the download where the vendor publishes one (Mojang's SHA-1, Wube's,
PaperMC's and Fabric's SHA-256, npm's integrity), or against the
vendor's signature (Forgejo and its runner); source builds are pinned by
tag and commit, apt packages by version from the index the InRelease
names that the role's pinned key signs, Debian's container template from
the index Proxmox's release key signs. Debian signs no sums of its cloud
builds; those are read over HTTPS. Every value a vendor gave is checked
against what its pin may hold (pins.WRITES: versions, hashes, file names,
addresses on the vendor's own host) before anything is written, since
Ansible templates the files that hold them. bump prints one line per
moved pin, `name: old -> new`, which .github/workflows/pins.yml puts in
the commit message.

Needs network access, git, gpg and gpgv, and uv for LiteLLM's lock.
"""

